Another day in the dungeon....

Maximus the lawful priest, cruising along, getting all sorts of nifty
stuff.. plate mail +0 on level 1, GoP on level 2 (magic lamp), CoP, +2
hard hat, hard shoes on level 3 (-8 AC on level 3 of the dungeon makes
things real easy). Later trip through the mines nets me +2 GDSM and a +3
Excaliber. Anyway...

Level 14, I find a chaotic altar. I'm carrying about 6 potions of water
and even more potions of blindness and sickess just waiting for that
unicorn horn I still don't have. And there it is... a BLACK UNICORN!!.
Whap! Whap! Grab the corpse, plunk it down on the altar, #offer...

A voice booms out "This action is an insult to chaos!!" Huan Ti zaps me
with a lightning bolt, but no dice, I've got shock resistance.
Undeterred, Huan Ti cuts loose with that wide-angle disintigration ray.
"You fry to a crisp" -more-
Do you wish to see your inventory? (y/n)

If I had just not have gotten that shock resistance from that stupid
black pudding I would have survived the whole fiasco... grrrrrr. I've
ascended several times, but this is the first time I've gotten
disintigrated merely from trying to convert an altar! Sheesh.

